return [
    'balloons-for-birthdays' => [
        ['How do I choose birthday balloon decor for the guest of honour’s age?', 'Start with the age, interests, venue, and way the space will be used. First birthdays often suit a soft cake-table backdrop, while children’s parties may need brighter themed decor and durable placement away from play areas. Teen and adult celebrations usually benefit from a cleaner photo feature, coordinated number balloons, or a statement garland. We scale the design so it feels appropriate for both the person and the room.'],
        ['Can a birthday balloon setup be personalized without using copyrighted characters?', 'Yes. A theme can be communicated through colour, shapes, props, numbers, patterns, and custom wording without copying a protected character. For example, a space, racing, princess, sports, or jungle-inspired celebration can use a distinctive palette and related visual details. Send us the invitation or mood board and we can translate its overall direction into original balloon decor that still feels clearly connected to the party.'],
        ['What information helps you design a milestone birthday display?', 'Tell us the age being celebrated, preferred colours, venue dimensions, guest count, main photo area, and whether the event includes a cake table, stage, or entrance feature. Inspiration images are helpful, but room photos are equally important because they show wall space, furniture, and access. For milestone birthdays, we can plan number balloons and signage as part of one balanced focal point rather than separate decorations.'],
        ['Which birthday balloon setup works best in a small home or condo?', 'A compact asymmetrical garland, a freestanding mini backdrop, or a coordinated number display usually gives the strongest visual result without blocking furniture or walkways. Ceiling height, elevator size, and building rules can affect the design. We use the room photos and available floor width to recommend a setup that creates a useful photo area while leaving comfortable space for guests, gifts, food, and children.'],
        ['How long before a birthday party should the balloons be installed?', 'Installation is normally planned to finish before guests or the photographer arrive. The exact window depends on the size of the setup, venue access, parking, elevators, and whether other vendors are working in the same area. Sharing the event start time and the earliest access time lets us build a realistic schedule. Outdoor installations may need a later setup because temperature, wind, and direct sunlight affect balloons.'],
        ['What affects the quote for custom birthday balloon decoration?', 'The main factors are the overall size, balloon quantity and finishes, structural supports, backdrop or prop rentals, personalization, installation time, travel, venue access, and removal requirements. A reference photo alone does not show the scale of your room, so include the event address and a photo or measurement of the setup area. We can then recommend a design level that fits the visual goal and available budget.'],
    ],
    'wedding-balloons' => [
        ['How can balloons be incorporated into a wedding without making the decor feel casual?', 'Wedding balloon decor feels refined when the palette is controlled, balloon sizes are balanced, and the installation relates to the architecture and floral plan. We often use muted neutrals, pearl or metallic accents, restrained asymmetry, and carefully placed floral details. Instead of decorating every surface, one intentional feature at the entrance, sweetheart table, stage, or photo area usually creates a more polished result.'],
        ['When should balloon decor be coordinated with the florist and venue designer?', 'Coordination should happen before finalizing the installation layout. Sharing the floral palette, backdrop dimensions, linen colours, floor plan, and vendor schedule helps prevent visual conflicts and duplicated structures. If flowers or draping will be attached near the balloons, the responsible vendors should agree on access and installation order. This creates one cohesive wedding design and reduces last-minute changes at the venue.'],
        ['Which wedding areas benefit most from a balloon installation?', 'The best location is usually an area guests will see or photograph repeatedly: the reception entrance, sweetheart table, stage, seating-chart display, dessert table, or dedicated portrait zone. The correct choice depends on the venue layout and existing decor. We consider camera angles, guest circulation, ceiling height, lighting, and table placement so the installation improves the room rather than hiding architectural or floral features.'],
        ['Can wedding balloons match an exact invitation or fabric colour?', 'We can work toward a close visual match using manufacturer colour charts, layered balloons, and complementary tones. Balloon material reflects light differently from paper, fabric, and digital screens, so an exact colour match cannot always be guaranteed. Providing physical swatches, professional palette references, or daylight photos is more reliable than a phone screenshot. We build a coordinated palette that looks consistent in the actual venue lighting.'],
        ['What venue details are needed before confirming wedding balloon decor?', 'We need the installation address, access window, loading and parking instructions, ceiling height, wall and attachment rules, room dimensions, and contact for the venue or planner. Please also share whether the feature must be freestanding and when it needs to be removed. Banquet halls often have strict vendor schedules, so confirming these details early protects the wedding timeline and helps us choose the right structure.'],
        ['Can the wedding balloon installation be removed after the reception?', 'Removal can be planned when the venue requires same-night teardown or when rental structures, backdrops, and signage are included. The quote should specify whether removal is required, the pickup window, and who can provide access after the event. Balloon disposal and rental collection are different tasks, so they need to be confirmed in advance. We coordinate the plan with the couple, venue, or planner before installation day.'],
    ],
    'corporate-event-balloons' => [
        ['How do you translate a company brand guide into balloon decor?', 'We review the approved logo, colour values, campaign graphics, event purpose, and examples of how the brand is normally presented. Balloon colours are then selected as the closest physical match, supported by neutral or secondary tones where needed. The layout can reflect the brand’s personality—minimal, energetic, premium, or playful—while keeping logos and key messages visible for photography and guest content.'],
        ['What should a business provide for a branded balloon installation?', 'Please provide the event date, venue contact, access schedule, floor plan or setup measurements, high-resolution logo files, brand colour references, and the intended use of the display. We also need to know whether signage is supplied by your team or produced as part of the decor. For approvals, identify one decision-maker who can confirm the palette and layout before materials and custom elements are prepared.'],
        ['How is decor for a grand opening different from decor for a corporate gala?', 'A grand opening usually needs strong street or entrance visibility, a clear ribbon-cutting area, and decor that frames signage without blocking the doorway. A gala or conference often needs a more controlled interior feature for registration, a stage, sponsor wall, or photographs. We design around the business goal, guest flow, media angles, safety clearances, and the length of time the display will remain in place.'],
        ['Can balloon decor accommodate multiple sponsors or campaign messages?', 'Yes, provided the visual hierarchy is agreed in advance. A backdrop or sign can reserve defined areas for the host brand, event title, and sponsor marks, while balloons frame rather than cover the graphics. Supply final approved artwork and usage rules before production. When many logos are involved, a simpler balloon palette often keeps the display professional and ensures the printed messaging remains readable in photos.'],
        ['What access information is important for office, retail, or convention venues?', 'Corporate installations often involve loading docks, security check-in, service elevators, certificates or vendor registration, restricted working hours, and public-area safety rules. Share the building contact and all access instructions before the event. We also need to know when flooring, signage, AV, and furniture will be installed so our work can be sequenced efficiently without delaying staff, other vendors, or the public opening.'],
        ['Can corporate balloon displays remain installed for several days?', 'Some air-filled displays can remain presentable beyond a single event, but suitability depends on balloon type, indoor temperature, sunlight, HVAC airflow, public contact, and venue policy. Tell us the full display period when requesting a quote. We can recommend materials and placement for the intended duration, explain realistic appearance changes, and identify whether maintenance, repositioning, or scheduled removal should be included.'],
    ],
    'anniversary-balloons' => [
        ['How can anniversary balloons reflect a specific milestone year?', 'The milestone can guide the palette and personalization without limiting the design to large numbers. Silver is traditionally associated with 25 years and gold with 50, while other anniversaries can use wedding colours, favourite tones, family photographs, names, or a meaningful date. We combine these references into a backdrop, garland, or dinner feature that feels personal to the couple rather than like a generic birthday display.'],
        ['Can you plan anniversary decor as a surprise for the couple?', 'Yes. A surprise setup requires one reliable contact who can approve the design, provide venue access, and keep the couple’s arrival time updated. Share any colours or flowers they dislike, the correct spelling of names, and the photography plan. For a home or restaurant surprise, we also confirm how long the room is available so installation can be completed discreetly before the couple enters.'],
        ['What works best for an intimate anniversary dinner?', 'For a smaller dinner, one well-composed focal point is usually more effective than decor throughout the room. A compact garland around a sign, a freestanding photo frame, or an elegant balloon-and-flower accent near the table can create atmosphere without interrupting service. We account for chair movement, servers, candles, windows, and restaurant rules when choosing the height and placement.'],
        ['Can family photos or the original wedding date be included in the display?', 'Yes. A printed sign, photo panel, timeline, or framed images can be incorporated when artwork and permissions are supplied in time. We plan balloon placement so important photographs and wording remain visible. Please send high-resolution files and exact names or dates for approval; personalized print pieces need more preparation than standard balloons and should be confirmed before the final production deadline.'],
        ['How do balloon and flower accents change the look of anniversary decor?', 'Floral accents soften the shapes of a garland and can connect the display to centrepieces, bouquets, or the couple’s original wedding style. The balance depends on whether you want balloons to lead the design or act as a frame for flowers and signage. Available flower type, colour, season, and whether fresh or artificial elements are appropriate should all be confirmed as part of the quote.'],
        ['What details are needed to quote an anniversary setup accurately?', 'Include the milestone year, event date and address, venue type, guest count, preferred palette, setup-area photo and measurements, access time, and any numbers, signs, flowers, or backdrop you want. If the celebration is a surprise, mention the arrival plan. These details allow us to price the actual scale, rentals, personalization, installation, travel, and possible removal instead of estimating from an inspiration image alone.'],
    ],
    'baby-shower-balloons' => [
        ['How do you build a baby shower palette when the parents do not want pink or blue?', 'A gender-neutral palette can be built from the venue, invitation, season, or nursery style. Sage, sand, cream, warm white, terracotta, muted yellow, lavender, and soft metallic accents can feel celebratory without signalling gender. We normally use several related tones and balloon sizes so the result has depth. Signage, florals, teddy-bear, cloud, botanical, or moon details can reinforce the theme.'],
        ['Should the baby’s name be included on a shower backdrop?', 'Only if the family wants it revealed. A backdrop can instead use a family surname, “Oh Baby,” “Baby in Bloom,” or another general message. If a name is included, provide the exact spelling and capitalization before production. We size the lettering for the backdrop and camera distance, then place balloons around it so the words stay readable in family photos and are not covered by the garland.'],
        ['What balloon setup works around a baby shower dessert table?', 'An asymmetrical garland or partial arch usually frames the table without competing with the cake and treats. We consider the table width, height of the cake stand, backdrop, signage, and where guests will queue. Balloons should not obstruct serving access or hang over uncovered food. A room photo and the dessert vendor’s table dimensions help us design the feature at the correct scale.'],
        ['Can baby shower decor be installed in a condo party room?', 'Yes, but the building’s booking hours, loading rules, elevator reservation, ceiling restrictions, and cleanup requirements should be checked first. Condo rooms often have limited setup time and fixed furniture, so a freestanding backdrop or compact garland may be more practical than a wide arch. Send photos of the actual room, not only the building listing, so we can account for its current layout.'],
        ['How can balloons support a shower theme without making it look too literal?', 'We can interpret the theme through palette, texture, silhouette, signage, and a few recognizable accents instead of using many themed props. For example, “baby in bloom” may use layered blush and botanical tones with restrained florals, while a cloud theme may use soft whites, pale blue, and rounded clusters. This approach keeps the decor elegant and lets the family, gifts, and dessert table remain central.'],
        ['When should baby shower balloon decor be booked?', 'Book once the date and venue are confirmed, particularly for weekends or a setup requiring a backdrop, custom sign, or florals. Early planning allows time to approve the palette and reserve rental pieces. To check availability, send the event address, start time, earliest access, approximate setup dimensions, and inspiration. Short-notice requests may be possible, but choices depend on materials and the existing installation schedule.'],
    ],
    'bridal-shower-balloons' => [
        ['How should bridal shower balloon decor differ from the wedding decor?', 'A bridal shower can have its own personality while still feeling connected to the wedding. Some clients borrow one wedding colour and make the shower lighter or more playful; others choose a completely separate brunch, garden, bow, pearl, or modern editorial theme. We avoid duplicating the main wedding installation and instead create an intimate focal point suited to gifts, conversation, desserts, and photographs with the bride.'],
        ['What is the best photo-area setup for a bridal shower?', 'A freestanding backdrop with an asymmetrical garland is versatile because it defines a portrait area without taking over the room. The ideal width depends on whether photos will include the bride alone, small groups, or the full bridal party. We also consider lighting, furniture, and guest circulation. Personalized wording should be short enough to remain visible when people stand in front of it.'],
        ['Can bridal shower balloons be styled for a restaurant brunch?', 'Yes. Restaurant decor should be compact, quick to install, and positioned so servers and guests can move comfortably. We confirm what may be attached to walls, the earliest access time, table plan, and whether the feature must be freestanding. A backdrop, welcome-sign garland, or restrained dessert-table accent often gives better photographs than multiple decorations spread around a busy dining room.'],
        ['How can flowers be added without overwhelming a bridal shower setup?', 'Flowers work best as intentional accents placed where they soften a garland or connect it to table arrangements. We coordinate the flower colour and scale with the balloons, backdrop, and room rather than filling every cluster. If another florist is involved, sharing the floral recipe or palette helps both vendors create one look. Availability and the choice between fresh and artificial elements are confirmed during quoting.'],
        ['What details can be personalized for the bride-to-be?', 'Options may include her name, future surname, initials, shower phrase, wedding date, or a palette based on the invitation. Personalized signage, bows, florals, pearl-like finishes, and small themed props can be incorporated into the main feature. Exact spelling and approved wording are required before production. We keep personalization readable and balanced so it enhances photographs rather than crowding the display.'],
        ['What should the host send when requesting a bridal shower quote?', 'Send the date, address, event and access times, venue photos, approximate installation width, theme or invitation, preferred colours, guest count, and any backdrop, flowers, signage, or table feature you want. Mention whether the venue requires insurance, elevator booking, or same-day removal. With this information we can recommend an appropriately scaled design and avoid suggesting decor that will not fit the room or schedule.'],
    ],
    'baptism-balloons' => [
        ['How can baptism balloon decor feel celebratory while remaining respectful?', 'We use a restrained palette, balanced placement, and meaningful details rather than an overly busy party theme. Soft white, ivory, blue, blush, sage, champagne, and subtle metallics can frame a cross, name, date, floral arrangement, or family photo area. The design is adjusted to the family’s tradition and reception setting so it feels appropriate for the occasion while still creating a warm celebration.'],
        ['Do you decorate inside a church or only the reception venue?', 'Most balloon installations are planned for the reception, restaurant, banquet room, home, or photo area after the ceremony. Decoration inside a place of worship depends entirely on its rules and approval. If church decor is requested, the family must confirm permitted locations, attachment methods, installation time, and removal requirements with the administrator before a design can be finalized. Freestanding decor may be the safest option.'],
        ['Can baptism decor include a cross, name, or ceremony date?', 'Yes. These elements can be incorporated through a backdrop, sign, panel, or carefully positioned prop. Provide exact spelling and date details for approval before production. We make sure balloons frame rather than cover religious symbols and lettering. The scale is planned for the photo distance and venue so the personalized information remains clear when the child, parents, godparents, and family stand in front.'],
        ['Is the same decor suitable for a christening or First Communion celebration?', 'Some visual elements can work across these occasions, but the wording, symbols, age of the child, and event format should guide the final design. A christening may use softer nursery-inspired styling, while First Communion decor often feels cleaner and more formal. Tell us the specific ceremony and family preferences so the palette, signage, and focal details are relevant rather than using a generic religious-event template.'],
        ['Where should a baptism backdrop be positioned at the reception?', 'Good locations include behind the dessert table, beside the family table, or in a separate portrait area with enough distance for group photos. It should not obstruct catering, emergency routes, high chairs, or guest seating. We use room photos and measurements to determine whether a compact backdrop, garland, or freestanding arch will create the strongest feature in the available space.'],
        ['What planning information is important for baptism balloon installation?', 'Share the ceremony and reception schedule, venue address, earliest room access, setup-area dimensions, building rules, palette, wording, and any cross, florals, backdrop, or dessert table involved. Because family celebrations may begin soon after the service, access timing is especially important. We plan installation around the venue schedule so decor is ready before guests arrive without interfering with catering or other preparations.'],
    ],
    'christmas-balloons' => [
        ['What Christmas balloon style works best for an office versus a private home?', 'Office and retail displays usually need a clear branded or seasonal focal point, durable placement, and open walkways for staff and customers. Home decor can be more intimate and coordinated with the tree, fireplace, dining area, or family photo space. We adjust scale, colour, and structure to the setting rather than applying the same red-and-green garland everywhere.'],
        ['Can a Christmas balloon display stay up throughout the holiday season?', 'Some indoor air-filled displays can last beyond a one-day party, but appearance depends on temperature, sunlight, heating vents, public contact, and the balloon finishes selected. Tell us the required start and end dates before design approval. We can recommend suitable placement and explain realistic longevity, maintenance, and removal needs. Long-term retail installations should be protected from doors, sharp merchandise, and heavy customer traffic.'],
        ['How can holiday decor match a company brand instead of traditional Christmas colours?', 'We can start with company colours and introduce one or two seasonal elements such as metallic accents, winter whites, stars, ornaments, or restrained greenery. This keeps the display recognizable as a holiday feature without losing the brand identity. Share approved brand colours and any restrictions on religious or seasonal language so signage and decor are appropriate for employees, customers, and campaign photography.'],
        ['What is a balloon Christmas tree and where does it work well?', 'A balloon Christmas tree is a sculptural, tree-shaped arrangement made from coordinated balloon clusters, sometimes with decorative accents. It can create a freestanding focal point in an office lobby, school, retail window, party room, or photo area where a traditional tree is not desired. Its footprint, height, stability, and public access must be planned for the actual location and duration.'],
        ['Are there safety considerations for Christmas decor in public spaces?', 'Yes. Decor must leave doors, aisles, exits, sprinklers, alarms, signage, and accessibility routes clear. It should also be positioned away from heaters, open flames, sharp fixtures, and areas where carts or crowds may damage it. The venue or property manager should approve the location and attachment method. For malls, offices, and schools, provide vendor access and safety requirements before installation.'],
        ['When should office and retail Christmas installations be reserved?', 'Holiday installation dates are concentrated in a short period, so businesses should enquire as soon as the campaign, party, or opening date is known. Include the desired installation duration, public opening hours, loading access, approval contact, brand palette, and removal date. Early confirmation provides more choice for custom signage and helps schedule installation outside customer or staff traffic when required.'],
    ],
    'valentines-day-balloons' => [
        ['How can Valentine’s Day balloon decor feel sophisticated rather than predictable?', 'A sophisticated design uses a focused palette, negative space, varied balloon sizes, and one strong visual message instead of covering the room with red hearts. Blush, burgundy, champagne, cream, black, or muted rose can create a more editorial mood. Flowers, fabric, lighting, or a minimal sign may be added selectively so the installation suits the person, restaurant, hotel, or brand.'],
        ['Can you install a romantic room surprise before the recipient arrives?', 'Yes, when the person booking can provide authorized access and a reliable arrival window. Hotels and rental properties may restrict outside vendors, adhesives, candles, or items placed on beds, so permission must be confirmed first. We coordinate with the booking contact or venue, protect the surprise, and plan enough time for installation and photography before the recipient enters the room.'],
        ['What should restaurants and retailers consider for a Valentine’s display?', 'The display should be visible and photo-friendly without narrowing entrances, covering products, or interrupting table service. We consider customer flow, brand colours, operating hours, fire routes, and how long the feature will remain installed. A compact entrance garland, branded photo backdrop, or window-adjacent installation often performs better than scattered decorations and gives customers a clear place to create social content.'],
        ['Can Valentine balloons be designed for a proposal without duplicating engagement decor?', 'Yes. The Valentine page focuses on seasonal styling and time-sensitive romantic surprises, while a proposal design is personalized around the actual question, location, and couple. We can combine Valentine colours with a custom message, but avoid making every setup identical. Share the proposal plan, photographer position, arrival route, and preferred level of privacy so the decor supports the moment.'],
        ['How do foil heart balloons and latex garlands behave differently?', 'Foil hearts provide clear symbolic shapes and reflective highlights, while latex balloons create volume, custom colour layering, and organic garland forms. They can be combined, but temperature and placement affect both materials. Foils may show reflections and seams in photographs; latex changes more visibly with heat or cold. We select the mix based on the room, desired style, duration, and camera angles.'],
        ['Why should Valentine’s Day decor be booked earlier than a normal weekday setup?', 'Demand is concentrated around one date, venues have limited access windows, and personalized signs or floral elements need preparation. Early booking helps secure an installation time that matches dinner, hotel check-in, store opening, or a surprise arrival. Send the address, access contact, desired completion time, colour direction, and setup dimensions. Last-minute availability may be limited even for a relatively compact display.'],
    ],
    'bar-mitzvah-balloons' => [
        ['How can Bar Mitzvah balloon decor be personalized for the celebrant?', 'We can build the design around the celebrant’s name or initials, chosen theme, favourite colours, interests, invitation, and venue style. Personalization may appear on a backdrop, welcome sign, photo feature, or dance-floor display. We keep wording legible and age-appropriate, then use balloons to frame the identity rather than cover it. Exact spelling and approved artwork are required before production.'],
        ['What decor works for both the formal and party portions of a Bar Mitzvah?', 'A versatile photo backdrop or entrance feature can bridge the family reception and the later celebration. More energetic colours or themed details can be concentrated near the dance floor, while dining and ceremony-adjacent areas remain cleaner. We review the event timeline, room transitions, lighting, and age mix so the decor supports each part of the day without needing a completely separate installation.'],
        ['Can balloon centrepieces be designed without blocking conversation?', 'Yes. Centrepieces should respect sightlines across the table and leave room for place settings, food service, table numbers, and floral pieces. We need table dimensions and the venue’s centrepiece limits before recommending a style. Low accents or carefully elevated elements can repeat the main palette while keeping guests comfortable. For crowded tables, decor around the room may be more effective than adding volume to every table.'],
        ['How should balloons be positioned near a dance floor or entertainment area?', 'Installations near entertainment zones need stable structures and clear separation from speakers, lighting, performers, cables, and active guest movement. A stage frame, DJ backdrop, or edge feature can define the area without hanging into the dance path. We coordinate with the venue and production team on dimensions and setup order, especially when AV equipment or special effects are involved.'],
        ['Can the balloon decor match a sports, music, gaming, or travel theme?', 'Yes. A theme can be expressed through a controlled palette, graphic backdrop, name treatment, shapes, and selected props. We aim for a cohesive event identity rather than filling the room with unrelated symbols. Provide the invitation, artwork, or examples of the celebrant’s interests, and identify any copyrighted logos that require permission. The final design is adapted to the venue and photography plan.'],
        ['What lead time is useful for a large Bar Mitzvah venue installation?', 'Begin planning once the venue and event schedule are confirmed. Larger events may require custom graphics, rental structures, loading coordination, security clearance, and collaboration with planners, florists, or AV teams. Send the floor plan, access hours, theme, guest count, key photo areas, and vendor contact early. This allows time for design approval and ensures installation fits the venue’s production schedule.'],
    ],
    'backdrop-rental' => [
        ['How do I choose the right backdrop size for my event?', 'Choose size according to the number of people in typical photos, ceiling height, available floor width, and camera distance. A backdrop for one or two guests can be compact, while family groups or corporate teams need more width and clear space in front. Send a straight-on room photo and measurements of the usable area. We will account for the stand, balloons, furniture, and guest circulation—not only the visible panel.'],
        ['Are your event backdrops freestanding, or must they attach to a wall?', 'Many backdrop configurations can be freestanding, which is helpful when venues prohibit wall attachments. The correct support depends on panel shape, height, balloons, signs, floor surface, and public access. Freestanding does not mean it can be placed anywhere; it still needs a stable, level footprint and clearance from exits and traffic. Venue rules and outdoor conditions must be reviewed before confirming the structure.'],
        ['What is included with a styled backdrop rental?', 'Inclusions depend on the selected package and may cover backdrop panels or fabric, supporting structure, installation, balloon styling, signage, florals or props, delivery, and scheduled pickup. Not every photo reference includes the same components. Your quote should list each rental and decorative element, the installation address, rental period, and removal plan so there is no ambiguity about what will be supplied.'],
        ['Can custom wording or a logo be added to a rental backdrop?', 'Yes, depending on the backdrop surface and production timeline. Names, dates, short phrases, event titles, and approved business logos may be produced as removable lettering or separate signage. High-resolution vector artwork is preferred for logos. Exact wording, capitalization, colour, and placement must be approved before production, and intellectual-property permission remains the client’s responsibility.'],
        ['What venue measurements and access details are needed for backdrop delivery?', 'Provide the usable width and ceiling height, doorway and elevator dimensions, stairs, loading location, parking, floor type, earliest access time, and required removal time. Also confirm whether the venue permits freestanding structures and where emergency routes are located. Large panels may not fit through residential doors or elevators as assembled, so accurate access information helps us select a setup that can be transported and installed safely.'],
        ['What happens to the backdrop after the event?', 'Rental backdrops and structural pieces remain the property of the supplier and must be collected at the agreed time and in their installed condition. Do not move, dismantle, write on, or attach items to them unless permission is provided. The quote should specify pickup timing, access contact, and any responsibility for damage or missing pieces. Balloon disposal or full decor removal should also be confirmed separately.'],
    ],
    'balloon-arch-garland' => [
        ['What is the practical difference between a balloon arch and a balloon garland?', 'An arch is designed to frame an opening, walkway, backdrop, or focal point and normally relies on a defined supporting shape. A garland is a flexible cluster arrangement that can run along a backdrop, table, wall, staircase, or sign. The best option depends on whether people need to pass through it, what may be attached at the venue, the available footprint, and the desired camera angle.'],
        ['How large should a balloon arch or garland be?', 'Scale should be based on the object being framed and the viewing distance, not a generic balloon count. An entrance arch must allow comfortable headroom and width, while a dessert-table garland should relate to the table and backdrop. Send measurements and a straight-on photo with the setup area marked. We then recommend proportions that look intentional without blocking signage, doors, guests, or service access.'],
        ['What is an organic balloon garland?', 'An organic garland uses mixed balloon sizes and irregular clustering to create a flowing, dimensional shape. “Organic” describes the composition, not biodegradable material. It can be compact and refined or full and dramatic depending on density and palette. A classic arch is usually more uniform and symmetrical. We recommend the style that best suits the event design, venue architecture, and available installation time.'],
        ['Can an arch or garland be installed when the venue prohibits adhesives?', 'Often yes, by using an approved freestanding frame, weighted base, or existing rental backdrop, but the solution depends on the location and design. Clients should not assume removable hooks are permitted; obtain the venue’s written attachment rules. We need floor space and access measurements to choose a structure. Additional supports can affect both the appearance and the quote.'],
        ['Are balloon arches suitable for outdoor events?', 'They can be used outdoors, but wind, heat, cold, rain, direct sunlight, rough ground, and sudden weather changes affect stability and appearance. Outdoor balloons may oxidize, expand, contract, or move more than indoor decor. We review the location, shade, anchoring options, event duration, and backup plan before confirming suitability. Severe conditions may require relocation, design changes, delayed installation, or cancellation for safety.'],
        ['Why do quotes for similar-looking garlands vary?', 'Two photographs can look similar while differing greatly in width, depth, balloon finishes, support structure, installation height, access, travel, and removal. Chrome or specialty colours, flowers, signs, and outdoor anchoring also change material and labour needs. For an accurate comparison, define the finished dimensions, location, included rentals, installation conditions, and removal—not simply the number of colours or an inspiration image.'],
    ],
    'balloon-ceiling-decor' => [
        ['What ceiling information do you need before approving balloon decor?', 'We need clear photos, ceiling height and material, room dimensions, lighting and HVAC locations, sprinkler and alarm positions, venue attachment rules, and how the ceiling can be accessed. Grid ceilings, exposed structures, smooth residential ceilings, and banquet halls require different methods. The venue must approve the proposed installation area, and some ceilings may not be suitable for attached or suspended decor.'],
        ['Can ceiling balloon decor be created without helium?', 'Yes, some effects can be achieved with air-filled balloons attached to an approved support or suspended using an appropriate method. Air-filled and helium-filled ceilings look different and have different installation needs. The choice depends on ceiling material, height, duration, venue policy, and access equipment. We do not confirm a method until photos and restrictions have been reviewed.'],
        ['How do sprinklers, smoke detectors, and HVAC affect a ceiling installation?', 'They require clear, code-compliant space and must never be covered, tied to, or obstructed. Air vents can also move ribbons and balloons or push them into restricted equipment. The venue or property manager should identify required clearances and approve the layout. If safe separation cannot be maintained, we may recommend a suspended feature over a defined area, a wall installation, or a freestanding alternative.'],
        ['Does a high ceiling make balloon decor more difficult?', 'Higher ceilings may require lifts, ladders, additional labour, longer installation time, and a larger amount of decor to remain visually effective from floor level. Access equipment must fit through the venue and be permitted on the floor. Provide the exact height and any equipment restrictions early. In some spaces, a lower hanging cloud or concentrated feature gives a better result than trying to cover the entire ceiling.'],
        ['How long can ceiling balloons remain in place?', 'Duration depends on whether balloons are air-filled or helium-filled, their size and finish, temperature, sunlight, HVAC, and the visual standard expected. Tell us whether the decor is for a few hours, overnight, or multiple days. We can recommend a suitable approach and discuss expected changes. Venue approval and a scheduled removal plan are required regardless of intended duration.'],
        ['How is ceiling balloon decor removed safely?', 'Removal should be planned with the same attention as installation, especially when ladders, lifts, suspended lines, or venue access are involved. Do not pull down decor or release balloons into the room. The quote should identify the removal window, access contact, equipment, and whether the venue requires immediate teardown. Rental supports and all attachment materials must also be collected according to the agreed plan.'],
    ],
    'graduation-balloons' => [
        ['How can graduation balloons accurately match school colours?', 'Provide an official colour reference, school website, invitation, gown photo, or physical swatch rather than relying on a general description such as “blue.” Balloon materials reflect light differently, so exact colour matching is not always possible, but we can build a close coordinated palette. Adding white, black, silver, or gold can help distinguish multiple school colours and make them photograph clearly.'],
        ['Can one display celebrate multiple graduates or programs?', 'Yes. A shared display can use a common class year with separate names, school colours, or program details. The layout needs a clear hierarchy so it does not become crowded. Send the exact spelling, credentials, and approved abbreviations for each graduate. For different schools, we can use neutral balloons to unify the design while assigning colour or signage zones to each person.'],
        ['What makes a graduation photo backdrop useful for cap-and-gown pictures?', 'It should be wide enough for the graduate and family, free of low elements that hide the gown, and positioned with flattering light and camera distance. The class year and name must remain visible behind people. We consider cap height, group size, furniture, and guest circulation when sizing the backdrop. A clean design often photographs better than many small themed details.'],
        ['Can graduation decor be installed at a school or ceremony venue?', 'Yes, when the school or venue authorizes the vendor, location, access time, attachment method, and safety plan. Ceremonies may have strict loading, security, stage, and teardown schedules. Provide the administrator’s contact and written requirements early. Freestanding entrance, stage-edge, or photo-area decor may be more practical than anything attached to school property.'],
        ['What should be considered for an outdoor graduation party?', 'Shade, wind, temperature, rain, ground surface, anchoring, and a weather backup location are essential. Direct sun can change balloon colour and size, while wind affects structures and photographs. We review the actual yard or venue rather than assuming a tent solves every issue. The design, installation time, and final go/no-go decision may need to change if conditions are unsafe.'],
        ['Why is graduation-season booking time-sensitive?', 'School ceremonies and family parties cluster on the same weekends, while custom names, class years, and school-colour materials require preparation. Once the date and venue are confirmed, send the access time, setup dimensions, graduate details, palette, and desired photo area. Early booking improves scheduling and rental availability; last-minute requests may need simpler personalization or a smaller installation.'],
    ],
    'engagement-balloons' => [
        ['How should proposal balloon decor be planned around the actual moment?', 'Start with where the proposer will stand, where the partner will enter, and where the photographer or phone camera will be positioned. The message and key decor should remain visible from that angle. We also consider lighting, music or candles, walking paths, and where personal items will be placed. A beautiful setup should guide the moment naturally without revealing the surprise too early.'],
        ['Can a “Marry Me” setup be installed secretly at a hotel or restaurant?', 'Yes, if the venue authorizes access and provides a staff contact who understands the surprise. Hotels and restaurants may restrict room entry, outside vendors, adhesives, flames, or setup during service. The person booking must coordinate permission and timing. We work to the approved access window and need a reliable update if the couple’s arrival changes.'],
        ['What is the difference between proposal decor and engagement-party decor?', 'Proposal decor is designed for one private, time-sensitive moment and a specific camera angle. Engagement-party decor must work for a longer gathering, guest circulation, group photos, food service, and a wider room. The same palette may be used, but the scale and placement are different. If both are planned, we can discuss whether any freestanding feature can transition to the celebration venue.'],
        ['How can an engagement setup include flowers, candles, or photographs?', 'These elements can create a more personal atmosphere when coordinated rather than added randomly. Flowers may soften a garland, photographs can be arranged in a timeline, and battery-operated candles may define the approach. Open flames and venue-provided candles require explicit permission. Share the photographer’s plan and any personal items early so the layout protects sightlines and keeps important details visible.'],
        ['What is the best backup plan for an outdoor proposal?', 'Reserve an indoor or sheltered alternative that can accommodate the decor and photographer. Wind, rain, heat, cold, public access, and changing light can affect balloons and installation safety. The backup decision needs a deadline and a person authorized to approve the move. We cannot guarantee an outdoor display will look or behave like an indoor reference when conditions change.'],
        ['What information can be shared without spoiling a surprise proposal?', 'One organizer can handle the address, access permission, arrival time, palette, message, and payment while keeping communications away from the recipient. Use a safe phone number and email, and tell us any words that should not appear in notifications. We still require exact spelling, venue approval, and a reachable day-of contact. Clear discreet coordination is more important than involving many people.'],
    ],
    'halloween-balloons' => [
        ['How can Halloween balloon decor be made fun for children instead of frightening?', 'Use friendly shapes, brighter orange, purple, green, or pastel tones, and recognizable details such as smiling ghosts, pumpkins, bats, or candy without realistic horror imagery. We tailor the level of “spooky” to the children’s ages and the host’s preferences. A colourful photo backdrop or entrance garland can communicate Halloween clearly while remaining welcoming for daycare, school, community, and family events.'],
        ['What creates a more sophisticated Halloween look for adults?', 'A limited palette such as black, smoke, burgundy, deep plum, bone, or metallic copper creates a stronger adult atmosphere than many novelty colours. Layered balloon sizes, dramatic asymmetry, fabric, lighting, or one sculptural prop can add depth. We keep the theme intentional and leave breathing room around signage, bars, dining tables, or lounge furniture so the decor feels styled rather than cluttered.'],
        ['Can a Halloween display be used in a shop or restaurant for several days?', 'Some indoor air-filled displays can be planned for a multi-day seasonal promotion, but their appearance depends on sunlight, HVAC, heat, public contact, and placement near doors or merchandise. Tell us the entire display period and business hours. We can recommend a durable location, protect walkways, and schedule installation or removal outside customer traffic where the property permits.'],
        ['How do props and balloons work together in a Halloween photo area?', 'Props should establish the scene while balloons frame it and add colour and volume. We plan where guests will stand, which elements must remain visible, and how the lighting affects dark colours. Too many small props can disappear in photographs, so one clear backdrop, sign, or focal object often works best. Any client-supplied props need dimensions and photos before the layout is approved.'],
        ['Is outdoor Halloween balloon decor practical in late October?', 'It depends on wind, temperature, rain, sunlight, installation surface, and the duration of the event. Cool weather can contract balloons and strong wind can make arches unsafe or visually unstable. We require an indoor or sheltered backup for uncertain conditions. The final design may use lower, more heavily supported elements rather than a tall entrance arch when exposure is high.'],
        ['What timing should schools and businesses allow for Halloween installation?', 'Allow time for vendor check-in, unloading, safe installation, and inspection before students, staff, or customers enter the area. Schools and commercial properties may require security registration, insurance, approved attachment methods, and strict removal times. Share these requirements with the event date, floor plan, and public opening schedule so the installation can be planned without disrupting normal operations.'],
    ],
    'balloon-and-flower-decoration' => [
        ['How do you decide the right balance between balloons and flowers?', 'The balance depends on the event style, backdrop, budget, and which material should lead the design. A romantic wedding feature may use restrained balloons with more floral texture, while a birthday garland may use flowers only as small transitions between colour groups. We consider scale from the camera’s viewpoint so flowers do not disappear and balloons do not overwhelm the softer details.'],
        ['Do you use fresh or artificial flowers with balloon installations?', 'Available options depend on the design, season, location, installation duration, and supplier availability. Fresh and artificial flowers behave differently and should not be assumed from an inspiration photo. During quoting, confirm the desired flower type and any specific varieties. If a separate florist is supplying stems, both vendors need to agree on quantities, preparation, installation responsibility, and timing.'],
        ['Can balloon-and-flower decor match an existing bridal bouquet or centrepiece?', 'Yes. Share the florist’s palette, flower list, ribbon or fabric swatches, and clear daylight images. We can select balloon tones and floral accents that coordinate without attempting to copy natural colours exactly. If the main florist is involved, early communication helps avoid conflicting shades and ensures flowers intended for the installation are prepared correctly for the required placement and duration.'],
        ['Are flower walls and floral balloon backdrops the same thing?', 'No. A flower wall is a surface covered primarily with flowers, while a floral balloon backdrop may use solid or fabric panels framed by balloons and selected flower clusters. They have different texture, weight, cost, transport, and installation requirements. We clarify which elements are included in the quote so a client requesting a few floral accents does not expect a fully covered flower wall.'],
        ['What allergy or venue concerns should be discussed before adding flowers?', 'Tell us about known flower, pollen, fragrance, or latex sensitivities and any venue restrictions on fresh plant material, water, soil, or loose petals. Some hospitals, care settings, food-service spaces, and cultural venues have specific rules. We can discuss alternative flower types or artificial accents where appropriate, but the client and venue should confirm that the selected materials meet their requirements.'],
        ['Why does balloon-and-flower decor require more planning than a balloon-only setup?', 'It involves coordinating two material systems with different sourcing, preparation, handling, and longevity. Specific flowers may be seasonal, custom structures may need added support, and installation order matters. Provide the palette, venue conditions, required duration, flower preference, backdrop dimensions, and access schedule early. This gives time to confirm availability and prevents last-minute substitutions that would change the intended look.'],
    ],
];
